                <pb facs="0514" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/588: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece (Morris) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-11-28T13:00:00+02:00">November 28, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 28—8:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. My 135, November 12 [<hi rendition="#italic">22</hi>], 7 p.m. International
                    Financial Commission presented November 26 note to Minister of Finance calling
                    for transfer of 30 percent interest on loans under its control. The American
                    1929, 4 percent loan was included in the list. I will telegraph Greek answer to
                    the Commission which is expected to be received tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
